Enable the DAB platform authenticator subsystem (ADR-0003)

ansible_base.authentication is vendored at the sources.lock DAB SHA but was not
in INSTALLED_APPS, so the whole platform authenticator surface was dead code in
the image: 15 authenticator plugins (local, ldap, saml, oidc, keycloak, azuread,
google_oauth2, github x6, radius, tacacs), the authenticator / authenticator_map
/ authenticator_user models with all five map types, the full trigger grammar,
and the /authenticators/, /authenticator_maps/, /authenticator_plugins/,
/trigger_definition/, /ui_auth/ endpoints.

Three changes, all required together:

1. awx/settings/defaults.py — add 'ansible_base.authentication' to INSTALLED_APPS.
   Nothing else is needed in settings: ansible_base.lib.dynamic_config.settings_logic
   keys off this app being installed (settings_logic.py:147) to append the
   AnsibleBaseAuth backend, insert SocialExceptionHandlerMiddleware +
   AuthenticatorBackendMiddleware ahead of django.contrib.auth's AuthenticationMiddleware,
   and prepend DAB's SessionAuthentication to DRF. URLs are likewise automatic:
   dynamic_urls walks INSTALLED_APPS for ansible_base.* apps exposing urls.py, and
   awx/urls.py already mounts its api_urls / api_version_urls / root_urls.

2. requirements/requirements_git.txt — add the `authentication` extra to the
   django-ansible-base pin. Without it social-auth-core, django-auth-ldap,
   python-ldap, ldap-filter, python3-saml, tacacs_plus, pyrad and xmlsec are absent
   and the plugins fail to import.

3. tools/ansible/roles/dockerfile/templates/Dockerfile.j2 — add openldap-devel and
   cyrus-sasl-devel to the builder stage and openldap to the runtime stage.
   python-ldap is sdist-only on PyPI, so it compiles at install time; upstream
   dropped the openldap headers when authentication moved to the gateway, and
   xmlsec1-devel/swig (already present) cover python3-saml but not LDAP.

Testing: built and verified on franken (see docs/design/ADR-0003). A fourth file,
pytest.ini, carries a narrow warning filter — the vendored-wheel bundle must be re-captured
once with egress (build/vendor/Dockerfile.capture, updated in the same commit) before
an airgap build can resolve the new dependencies, and the 18 authentication
migrations must be applied to an existing database.

Related: docs/design/ADR-0003-platform-authenticators.md, ADR-0002 (which this
consciously qualifies), docs/design/PARITY-LEDGER.md.
